	(text "6N137 is fast enough for 115200 baud. The TLP521 /\nPC817 already in stock are NOT - do not substitute\nthem without measuring first (O-6).\n\nOPEN - NOT FIXED HERE: this RX path INVERTS. The LED\nconducts when RO is HIGH, and an enabled 6N137 pulls its\noutput LOW with the LED on, so an idle mark reaches the\nCH340C as a continuous break. Telemetry cannot work as\ndrawn. The fix is a part change, not a rewire: swapping the\nLED round makes RO SINK the current, and the SP3485 RO\ndrive limits are not in hand. Needs the datasheet or a\ndigital isolator - O-21, review owner."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240.0000 245.0000 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.35 1.35)
				(thickness 0.20)
				(bold no)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bb8d0c0-98b3-4487-a696-c9bdb3c16c5d")
	)
